WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.840
- [Narrator] Sweden wants to
join NATO as soon as possible.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.940
The Nordic country
applied for a membership

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.370
at the same time as Finland last year,

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:10.140
shortly after Russia launched

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.720
its full-scale invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.300
But while Finland was accepted this April,

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.810
Turkey, and Hungary are
blocking Sweden from joining.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.240
Let's look at what's
holding up the process

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.573
and what Sweden can bring to
the Western Military Alliance.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.450
Sweden is strategically located

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.763
next to NATO's newest member Finland.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.670
If Sweden joined NATO,

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.050
troops would be able to go through

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.120
Swish territory into Finland,

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.300
to defend the 800-mile-long
border with Russia.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:42.780
- Those two countries, along
with Norway and Denmark,

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.450
formal type of Nordic
fortress in Northern Europe,

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.881
which helps NATO sure up
its defenses against Russia,

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:53.881
both over land, but also
at sea, in the Baltic Sea.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.910
- [Narrator] The Baltic Sea is
the shortest direct waterway

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.590
from Russia to the West.

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:01.950
This is where Sweden's,
Gotland Island is located.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.620
NATO often conducts
military exercises here,

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.480
and the island could be used as a base

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.600
to protect its naval
forces in Northern Europe.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:10.433
- By joining nato,

00:01:10.433 --> 00:01:14.100
Sweden also reinforces the
alliance with weaponry.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.080
It has surface-to-air missiles,

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.420
which will help NATO
bolsters its defenses,

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.640
its air defenses in this region.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.610
In addition, Sweden also has submarines

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:24.900
for the Baltic Sea,

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.270
and have a deep knowledge
of Russian affairs

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:30.420
having been so closely located
to Russia for over decades.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.330
In a way that many
European countries haven't.

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:36.000
- [Narrator] For centuries,
Sweden avoided taking part

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.740
in military conflicts,

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.360
but the country has worked closely

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.100
with the alliance in the past.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.140
- Sweden has had a close
partnership with NATO

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:47.340
for several decades, going
back to the mid-1990s

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.160
where Sweden was part of the NATO mission

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:51.930
in Bosnia Herzegovina,

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:52.920
and then since then,

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:57.920
it has participated in various
NATO missions in Afghanistan,

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.820
and it's been part of what's called

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:02.610
an Enhanced Opportunity Partnership.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:03.780
- [Narrator] But Russia's invasion

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:06.390
of Ukraine in February 2022,

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:10.350
made Sweden rethink its
policy of non-alignment.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:13.740
Russia opposes NATO membership
for Sweden and Finland,

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:16.020
and said, "This would have consequences."

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:18.450
- Swedish and Finnish
intelligence services

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.540
are prepared for increased cyber attacks,

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:22.920
increased espionage.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:26.070
They say they're not concerned
about direct military action

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:26.970
at the moment,

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:29.790
but Russia has threatened both countries

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.340
that there would be
consequences if they join NATO.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.290
- [Narrator] Every NATO member

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:37.740
needs to approve Sweden's
application to join,

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.440
Hungary and Turkey are against it.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.380
Hungary's Parliament says
it's because of what it calls

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:47.130
unwarranted Swedish criticism
of its democratic record.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:49.080
While Turkey accuses Sweden

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.420
of sheltering Kurdish militants

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:54.060
that Ankara reconsiders
to be terrorists.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.830
- Sweden made a number of concessions

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:57.570
to Turkey to address these concerns,

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:01.050
including passing a new
anti-terrorism law in Parliament

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:03.270
that made it illegal to be a member

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:04.800
of a terrorism organization.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.200
And that includes the PKK,

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.730
which is a Turkish militant group

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:12.294
that Sweden also labels as
a terrorist organization.

00:03:12.294 --> 00:03:13.140
(crowd chanting)

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:15.630
- [Narrator] Hundreds of
people protested in Stockholm

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:17.010
against the new law

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.110
saying, "The Swedish Government is bowing

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:20.487
to Turkish pressure."

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:24.060
Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdoğan

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:26.580
asked Sweden to stop the protests

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.593
before he can agree to their membership.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:30.780
NATO's Secretary General

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:33.390
called a meeting with Sweden and Turkey

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:35.520
to try and sort out the issues

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:39.153
before the Alliance holds its
Summit in Lithuania in July.

00:03:40.187 --> 00:03:42.937
(dramatic music)

